    "https://manchester.unh.edu/student-experience/about-our-city": {
      "title": "About Our City",
      "description": "About Our City | UNH Manchester Skip to main content This site uses cookies to enhance your browsing experience. By continuing to use this site, you agree to the use of cookies, in accordance with the USNH website Privacy Policy. OK ✓ University of New Hampshire Search Menu Search UNH.edu Search UNH Manchester Search UNH.edu Search Search Commonly Searched Items: Academic Calendar Visit Tuition Registrar UNH Manchester Academics Programs of Study Graduate Programs Academic Advising Academic Support Academic Calendar Course Schedule Millyard Scholars Program Registration Office Departments Non-Degree Students Admissions How to Apply First-Year Students Transfer Students International Students Graduate Students Military & Veteran Students Financial Aid Tuition & Costs Scholarships Campus Tours & Events Accepted Students Careers Career and Professional Success Work-Based Learning Handshake Career Technology For Employers Wildcat Way to Professional Success Research Biotechnology Innovation Center Library NASA STEM on Station Undergraduate Research Winter Symposium Student Experience About Our City Assistant Dean of Student Success Campus Safety Commencement Clubs & Organizations Current Students Diversity & Inclusion Housing & Dining Student Wellness Student and Community Engagement Wildcats at the YMCA Basic Needs Support About Contact Us Directions & Parking Faculty & Staff Resources Leadership People Technology Blog Alumni Outreach STEM Discovery Lab Manchester CREATES STEM-MoBILE Student Experience About Our City In This Section Student Experience About Our City Assistant Dean of Student Success Campus Safety Commencement Clubs & Organizations Current Students Diversity & Inclusion Housing & Dining Student Wellness Student and Community Engagement Wildcats at the YMCA Basic Needs Support About Our City Home to more than 110,000 residents, Manchester is New Hampshire’s largest city and a place where students can learn, work, and build community. The historic Millyard, once home to bustling textile mills, now houses classrooms, labs, and innovative companies, creating a unique environment where education and industry intersect. For students who are just starting college, transferring, or returning to school, Manchester offers both opportunity and flexibility. A walkable downtown filled with local restaurants, shops, and cultural spaces sits just steps from campus, making it easy to balance academics with everyday life. With internships, community connections, and career pathways woven into the city itself, Manchester becomes more than a place to study, it’s a place to grow. Make the city your campus Manchester is more than where you study, it’s where you connect. Dive into local arts, culture, food, and events that bring the community together. The Currier Museum of Art An internationally renowned art museum. The Currier Museum of Art Wildcats at the YMCA Build a healthy spirit, mind, and body. Wildcats at the YMCA Palace Theatre Non-profit performing arts center. Palace Theatre Dining in Manchester More than 80 cafes, restaurants, diners, and eateries. Dining in Manchester SNHU Arena Indoor events arena from music, to sports, and more. SNHU Arena NH Fisher Cats Minor league baseball team. NH Fisher Cats Ranking and Reports College Raptor “Hidden Gem in the New England Region” (2021) College Raptor LIVABILITY.COM \"One of the best places to live in the US\" (2019) LIVABILITY.COM NH Magazine \"Next Cool City\" (2018) NH Magazine National Geographic \"Happiest Cities in the U.S.\" (2017) National Geographic New York Times \"A Millyard Transitions From Textiles to Tech\" (2017) New York Times Politico \"How a 19th-Century Town Became a New Millennium Marvel\" (2016) Politico Harvard Magazine \"Art, history, and eclectic restaurants—less than an hour away\" (2015) Harvard Magazine Quicklinks Programs of Study First Year Applicants Graduate Students Transfer Students International Students Veterans & Non-Tradit