    "https://manchester.unh.edu/student-experience/student-wellness": {
      "title": "Student Wellness",
      "description": "Student Wellness | UNH Manchester Skip to main content This site uses cookies to enhance your browsing experience. By continuing to use this site, you agree to the use of cookies, in accordance with the USNH website Privacy Policy. OK ✓ University of New Hampshire Search Menu Search UNH.edu Search UNH Manchester Search UNH.edu Search Search Commonly Searched Items: Academic Calendar Visit Tuition Registrar UNH Manchester Academics Programs of Study Graduate Programs Academic Advising Academic Support Academic Calendar Course Schedule Millyard Scholars Program Registration Office Departments Non-Degree Students Admissions How to Apply First-Year Students Transfer Students International Students Graduate Students Military & Veteran Students Financial Aid Tuition & Costs Scholarships Campus Tours & Events Accepted Students Careers Career and Professional Success Work-Based Learning Handshake Career Technology For Employers Wildcat Way to Professional Success Research Biotechnology Innovation Center Library NASA STEM on Station Undergraduate Research Winter Symposium Student Experience About Our City Assistant Dean of Student Success Campus Safety Commencement Clubs & Organizations Current Students Diversity & Inclusion Housing & Dining Student Wellness Student and Community Engagement Wildcats at the YMCA Basic Needs Support About Contact Us Directions & Parking Faculty & Staff Resources Leadership People Technology Blog Alumni Outreach STEM Discovery Lab Manchester CREATES STEM-MoBILE Student Experience Student Wellness In This Section Student Experience About Our City Assistant Dean of Student Success Campus Safety Commencement Clubs & Organizations Current Students Diversity & Inclusion Housing & Dining Student Wellness Student and Community Engagement Wildcats at the YMCA Basic Needs Support Student Wellness Our goal is to cultivate an environment that promotes, advocates for, and supports the individual and collective wellbeing of our students. We offer a range of services and resources both on and off campus to help foster life skills for a healthy emotional and mental outlook. Previous Slide Next Slide Need help now? If you or someone you know is experiencing a mental health emergency, please call 911 immediately. For urgent emotional support that is not life-threatening, TimelyCare's CrisisNow line is available 24/7 at 833-721-2255. No sign-up or wait required. Supporting Your Whole Self From mental health to everyday stress, explore the support and resources available to help you thrive during your time at UNH Manchester. On-Campus Mental Health Counseling UNH Manchester has partnered with The Mental Health Center of Greater Manchester (MHCGM) to offer in-person counseling services, including: Free, confidential screening and consultation with a licensed mental health therapist Referrals to mental health or substance misuse treatment Assistance in understanding how to afford additional treatment (with or without insurance) as well as identifying free services Schedule an appointment TimelyCare - 24/7 Access to Virtual Care UNH Manchester has partnered with TimelyCare to give you free, 24/7 access to virtual well-being and mental health support. Access TimelyCare Whether you're feeling overwhelmed, need someone to talk to, or are facing a mental health crisis, TimelyCare connects you with the care you need. To get started, visit timelycare.com/unhm or download the TimelyCare app and register with your UNH email address. TimelyCare Services, Support That Meets You Where You Are 24/7 Mental Health Support CrisisNow CrisisNow is phone-based mental health support when facing urgent emotional challenges. There is no sign-up, no wait, just call and connect with a trained counselor in only a few seconds. UNH Manchester CrisisNow line: 833-721-2255 TalkNow TalkNow is designed for everyday emotional support and stress management — think late-night anxiety, academic pressure, loneliness, or just needing someone to talk to. It connects you with a master's-level mental health professional in about 4 minutes on average through the TimelyCare app, and sessions are approximately 30 minutes. It's great for in-the-moment support that isn't necessarily an emergency. Scheduled Support & Self-Help Scheduled Counseling : Take control of your mental health journey by scheduling a counseling session on your own terms — choose the day, time, and provider that works best for you. Self-Care Content : Whenever you need a moment to recharge, access a library of self-care tools and resources 24/7, including meditation and yoga sessions, expert articles, and helpful videos to support your overall well-being. Peer Community: You're not alone in what you're going through. Connect with other students in an anonymous, judgment-free space where you can share, support, and be supported by peers who truly get it. TimelyCare Frequently Asked Questions expand all How do I access TimelyCare? Go to timelycare.com/unhm or directly download the TimelyCare app from the app store to register with your UNH email address. You can then start visits from any web-enabled device – smartphone, tablet, laptop, or desktop – anywhere in the United States. Who can use TimelyCare? Any UNH Manchester student enrolled in a degree program. Are there mental health appointments available in-person? We recognize that some students prefer in-person mental health support. In addition to TimelyCare, we offer in-person mental health services. See the top of this page for more information on on-campus mental health services and to book an in-person appointment with a licensed clinician. Wildcats for Recovery Wildcats for Recovery is a UNH campus initiative to support students with substance use challenges. Wildcats for Recovery is a community open to any UNH students, individuals in recovery, and recovery allies alike. We encourage any UNH student looking to explore their relationship with substances, with loved ones who struggle with substance use, or individuals simply looking to connect without the influence of alcohol or other drugs, to check out our peer support group, or attend one of our programming or tabling events throughout the semester.  UNH Manchester will be offering weekly Wildcats for Recovery peer recovery meet ups on campus open to all students. No preregistration or fees are required to attend Wildcats for Recovery peer groups and events. Mental Health Resources More than 80 percent of college students feel overwhelmed during the academic year, according to statistics from the National Alliance on Mental Illness (NAMI). Anxiety, depression and other mental illnesses are increasingly common on college campuses—and seeking help when you need it has never been more important. At UNH, wellness can help you achieve academic and personal success while at school and in your future. Wellness is the key to many aspects of our overall well-being, including: Academic achievement Personal growth and confidence Career fulfillment Social connection within the UNH community In other words, the better your wellness, the better your ability to thrive at UNH and beyond! UNH Wellness Resources Quicklinks Programs of Study First Year Applicants Graduate Students Transfer Students International Students Veterans & Non-Traditional Stop Campus Hazing Act More to Explore Academics Clery Report Emergency Procedures Program Consumer Information Event Calendar Faculty & Staff Resources Incident Report Form Copyright © 2026, University of New Hampshire. All rights reserved. TTY Users: 7-1-1 or 800-735-2964 (Relay NH) USNH Privacy Policies  • USNH Terms of Use  • Accessibility  • Statement of Nondiscrimination  • Jeanne Clery Act Contact Us UNH Manchester 88 Commercial Street Manchester, NH 03101 (603) 641-4101 +1 (603) 641-4304 UNH Manchester Academics Show Academics submenu Programs of Study Graduate Programs Academic Advising Show Academic Advising submenu Advising Appointments Advising Forms Foundations of Success Track Frequently Asked Questions Graduate Student Advising New Students Study Abroad & Away Parents and Families Show Parents and Families submenu Curriculum and Policy for Parents Navigating the Transition to College: A Timeline Parent and Family FAQ Academic Support Academic Calendar Course Schedule Millyard Scholars Program Registration Office Show Registration Office submenu Course Delivery Modality Glossary Grade Rules Graduation Show Graduation submenu Commencement Honors Convocation Hooding January Term Summer Session Transcripts Departments Non-Degree Students Admissions Show Admissions submenu How to Apply Show How to Apply submenu Check the Status of Your Application First-Year Students Transfer Students Show Transfer Students submenu Community College Students Previously Enrolled Students International Students Graduate Students Military & Veteran Students Show Military & Veteran Students submenu Military & Veteran Services Financial Aid Show Financial Aid submenu Apply for Aid Types of Aid Show Types of Aid submenu Summer Aid Work Study Resources Scholarships Loan Requirements Tuition & Costs Show Tuition & Costs submenu New England Regional Student Program Student Accounts Show Student Accounts submenu Refunds Scholarships Campus Tours & Events Accepted Students Careers Show Careers submenu Career and Professional Success Work-Based Learning Handshake Career Technology For Employers Wildcat Way to Professional Success Research Show Research submenu Biotechnology Innovation Center Library NASA STEM on Station Undergraduate Research Show Undergraduate Research submenu Undergraduate Research Conference Funding Your Research Winter Symposium Student Experience Hide Student Experience submenu About Our City Assistant Dean of Student Success Show Assistant Dean of Student Success submenu Care Team Campus Safety Show Campus Safety submenu Safety and Storm Closing Commencement Clubs & Organizations Current Students Diversity & Inclusion Housing & Dining Student Wellness Student and Community Engagement Wildcats at the YMCA Basic Needs Support About Show About submenu Contact Us Show Contact Us submenu Rent Our Space Directions & Parking Faculty & Staff Resources Show Faculty & Staff Resources submenu Business Office Event Resources Faculty Academic Resources Show Faculty Academic Resources submenu Academic Alerts Human Resources Show Human Resources submenu Employee Orientation Marketing & Communications Facilities Leadership Show Leadership submenu College Advisory Board People Show People submenu Emeriti Technology Blog Alumni Outreach Show Outreach submenu STEM Discovery Lab Show STEM Discovery Lab submenu STEM Programs and Resources for Teachers Manchester CREATES Show Manchester CREATES submenu Annual Report 2025 Annual Report 2024 Manchester Tech Camp Show Manchester Tech Camp submenu Parent Forms Faculty Tech for Teachers Institute Show Tech for Teachers Institute submenu Research Information Evaluation Report STEM-MoBILE Show STEM-MoBILE submenu Available Programming Sponsorships Apply Give Request Information myUNH"
