    "https://manchester.unh.edu/student-experience/student-community-engagement": {
      "title": "Student and Community Engagement",
      "description": "Student and Community Engagement | UNH Manchester Skip to main content This site uses cookies to enhance your browsing experience. By continuing to use this site, you agree to the use of cookies, in accordance with the USNH website Privacy Policy. OK ✓ University of New Hampshire Search Menu Search UNH.edu Search UNH Manchester Search UNH.edu Search Search Commonly Searched Items: Academic Calendar Visit Tuition Registrar UNH Manchester Academics Programs of Study Graduate Programs Academic Advising Academic Support Academic Calendar Course Schedule Millyard Scholars Program Registration Office Departments Non-Degree Students Admissions How to Apply First-Year Students Transfer Students International Students Graduate Students Military & Veteran Students Financial Aid Tuition & Costs Scholarships Campus Tours & Events Accepted Students Careers Career and Professional Success Work-Based Learning Handshake Career Technology For Employers Wildcat Way to Professional Success Research Biotechnology Innovation Center Library NASA STEM on Station Undergraduate Research Winter Symposium Student Experience About Our City Assistant Dean of Student Success Campus Safety Commencement Clubs & Organizations Current Students Diversity & Inclusion Housing & Dining Student Wellness Student and Community Engagement Wildcats at the YMCA Basic Needs Support About Contact Us Directions & Parking Faculty & Staff Resources Leadership People Technology Blog Alumni Outreach STEM Discovery Lab Manchester CREATES STEM-MoBILE Student Experience Student and Community Engagement In This Section Student Experience About Our City Assistant Dean of Student Success Campus Safety Commencement Clubs & Organizations Current Students Diversity & Inclusion Housing & Dining Student Wellness Student and Community Engagement Wildcats at the YMCA Basic Needs Support Student and Community Engagement Engage. Succeed. Belong The Office of Student and Community Engagement fosters a welcoming and inclusive campus where students and the UNH Manchester community feel a strong sense of belonging, community, and engagement. We empower students to thrive academically, socially, and personally through meaningful programs, wellness resources, and partnerships that support holistic success. By celebrating all identities and building connections, we create a culture of care that supports retention, development, and civic responsibility. Contact Office of Student and Community Engagement Second floor, Learning and Engagement Center Visit Pandora Net to see upcoming events, clubs and organizations, and how to get involved on campus. Pandora net Get involved! Campus Jobs Looking for a way to earn money, build your resume, and get involved on campus? UNH students can explore a variety of on-campus employment opportunities through the Workday job board. Keep in mind: Search by campus to be sure you’re finding employment at your desired location. The recruitment period for most UNH Manchester campus leadership jobs is in the spring semester for the following academic year. Student Job Board Student Activities The Office of Student and Community Engagement creates events, activities, and collaborates with other campus offices and clubs to provide fun ways to get involved at UNH Manchester. Want to know what's happening on campus? Simply read the weekly editions of The Flush found in campus restrooms, take a look at flyers around campus, or swing by the Student Commons! Pandora Net Start a Club It’s easy to start your own club on the UNH Manchester campus – all you need is the following: A unique idea that positively contributes to the UNHM campus Yourself and 2 other students A faculty or staff advisor If you're ready for the commitment of club leadership, simply click the link below to complete the Organization Registration form and review the current club policies. Your submission will be reviewed by the Office of Student and Community Engagement. If your club is approved, you will be contacted to set up an Introductory Meeting. Club Recognition Form Meet the Team Donna Laferriere Administrative Assistant II Email: Donna.Laferriere@unh.edu Phone: (603) 641-4113 Dana Pierce Manager of Events Email: Dana.Pierce@unh.edu Phone: (603) 641-4348 Ally Twitchell Coordinator of Student Involvement Email: Ally.Twitchell@unh.edu Phone: (603) 641-4165 Quicklinks Programs of Study First Year Applicants Graduate Students Transfer Students International Students Veterans & Non-Traditional Stop Campus Hazing Act More to Explore Academics Clery Report Emergency Procedures Program Consumer Information Event Calendar Faculty & Staff Resources Incident Report Form Copyright © 2026, University of New Hampshire. All rights reserved. TTY Users: 7-1-1 or 800-735-2964 (Relay NH) USNH Privacy Policies  • USNH Terms of Use  • Accessibility  • Statement of Nondiscrimination  • Jeanne Clery Act Contact Us UNH Manchester 88 Commercial Street Manchester, NH 03101 (603) 641-4101 +1 (603) 641-4304 UNH Manchester Academics Show Academics submenu Programs of Study Graduate Programs Academic Advising Show Academic Advising submenu Advising Appointments Advising Forms Foundations of Success Track Frequently Asked Questions Graduate Student Advising New Students Study Abroad & Away Parents and Families Show Parents and Families submenu Curriculum and Policy for Parents Navigating the Transition to College: A Timeline Parent and Family FAQ Academic Support Academic Calendar Course Schedule Millyard Scholars Program Registration Office Show Registration Office submenu Course Delivery Modality Glossary Grade Rules Graduation Show Graduation submenu Commencement Honors Convocation Hooding January Term Summer Session Transcripts Departments Non-Degree Students Admissions Show Admissions submenu How to Apply Show How to Apply submenu Check the Status of Your Application First-Year Students Transfer Students Show Transfer Students submenu Community College Students Previo