    "https://manchester.unh.edu/student-experience/wildcats-at-the-ymca": {
      "title": "Wildcats",
      "description": "Wildcats at the YMCA | UNH Manchester Skip to main content This site uses cookies to enhance your browsing experience. By continuing to use this site, you agree to the use of cookies, in accordance with the USNH website Privacy Policy. OK ✓ University of New Hampshire Search Menu Search UNH.edu Search UNH Manchester Search UNH.edu Search Search Commonly Searched Items: Academic Calendar Visit Tuition Registrar UNH Manchester Academics Programs of Study Graduate Programs Academic Advising Academic Support Academic Calendar Course Schedule Millyard Scholars Program Registration Office Departments Non-Degree Students Admissions How to Apply First-Year Students Transfer Students International Students Graduate Students Military & Veteran Students Financial Aid Tuition & Costs Scholarships Campus Tours & Events Accepted Students Careers Career and Professional Success Work-Based Learning Handshake Career Technology For Employers Wildcat Way to Professional Success Research Biotechnology Innovation Center Library NASA STEM on Station Undergraduate Research Winter Symposium Student Experience About Our City Assistant Dean of Student Success Campus Safety Commencement Clubs & Organizations Current Students Diversity & Inclusion Housing & Dining Student Wellness Student and Community Engagement Wildcats at the YMCA Basic Needs Support About Contact Us Directions & Parking Faculty & Staff Resources Leadership People Technology Blog Alumni Outreach STEM Discovery Lab Manchester CREATES STEM-MoBILE Student Experience Wildcats at the YMCA In This Section Student Experience About Our City Assistant Dean of Student Success Campus Safety Commencement Clubs & Organizations Current Students Diversity & Inclusion Housing & Dining Student Wellness Student and Community Engagement Wildcats at the YMCA Basic Needs Support Wildcats at the YMCA Student Discount at The Granite YMCA UNH Manchester has partnered with The Granite YMCA to get undergraduate and graduate students a highly discounted Y membership. From fitness equipment to group exercise classes, indoor and outdoor pools to tennis and basketball courts — for just $50 per semester, you can take advantage of all The Granite YMCA has to offer at any of its five locations. Just a 10-minute walk from UNH Manchester, think of the YMCA of Downtown Manchester as an extension of our campus. Give your brain a break with a fitness class or get a change of scenery by bringing your homework to the member lounge, complete with free Wi-Fi. Learn more below . YMCA Membership Contact: Phone: (603) 623-3558 Email: rdurand@graniteymca.org Visit the YMCA for more information expand all Get Your Membership All University of New Hampshire at Manchester students are eligible for a discounted membership to the five locations of The Granite YMCA. Students must sign up for the 2024-2025 academic year by October 1, 2024 (fall) or February 25, 2025 (spring) in order to receive the discounted rates. Students that sign up for the fall semester must visit the YMCA a minimum of eight times in order to maintain their discounted rate for the spring semester. Fill out your membership application below and bring it to the front desk of The Granite YMCA. Undergraduate Application Graduate Application Group Exercise & Pool Schedules Check out the group fitness and pool schedules by selecting your YMCA branch from the dropdown menu. Bring a Buddy Share your Y experience with a friend or family member! To use this free guest pass , please bring your guest and their photo ID to the front desk of The Granite YMCA. Limitations and restrictions apply. Please contact Ruthie Durand at 603-623-3558  or rdurand@graniteymca.org with any questions. Tuition Grant for Granite YMCA Employees Through this partnership, UNH Manchester provides employees of The Granite YMCA with a 10% tuition grant towards part- or full-time enrollment in any undergraduate program and select graduate programs. Tuition grant is only available to full-time, part-time and seasonal employees of The Granite YMCA, not to dependents or family members. Tuition grant may be used for undergraduate continuing education courses offered by UNH Manchester. Students wishing to enroll full-time must apply and be accepted to UNH Manchester or UNH Graduate School at Manchester to be considered for the tuition grant. To receive the tuition discount, each student must complete the Community Partnership Tuition Program verification form and submit it to the Student Financial Services office each semester. Once approved, UNH Manchester will adjust your tuition charges to the discounted rate. Check out our course schedule , or contact our Office of Admissions for more information. Quicklinks Programs of Study First Year Applicants Graduate Students Transfer Students International Students Veterans & Non-Traditional Stop Campus Hazing Act More to Explore Academics Clery Report Emergency Procedures Program Consumer Information Event Calendar Faculty & Staff Resources Incident Report Form Copyright © 2026, University of New Hampshire. All rights reserved. TTY Users: 7-1-1 or 800-735-2964 (Relay NH) USNH Privacy Policies  • USNH Terms of Use  • Accessibility  • Statement of Nondiscrimination  • Jeanne Clery Act Contact Us UNH Manchester 88 Commercial Street Manchester, NH 03101 (603) 641-4101 +1 (603) 641-4304 UNH Manchester Academics Show Academics submenu Programs of Study Graduate Programs Academic Advising Show Academic Advising submenu Advising Appointments Advising Forms Foundations of Success Track Frequently Asked Questions Graduate Student Advising New Students Study Abroad & Away Parents and Families Show Parents and Families submenu Curriculum and Policy for Parents Navigating the Transition to College: A Timeline Parent and Family FAQ Academic Support Academic Calendar Course Schedule Millyard Scholars Program Registration Office Show Registration Office submenu Course Delivery Modality Glossary Grade Rules Graduation